<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8"> <!--sets the characters-->
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"> <!--adjusts the layout for screen size-->

    <title>Florida</title>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="FinalFloridaCSS.css"> <!--imports the stylesheet-->
</head>

<body id="top"> <!--sets the location that the back to top button brings the user to-->

    <header> <!--The header portion of the page with an image and blurb-->

        <div class="container" onclick="myFunction(this)"> <!--code for the navbar at the top left of the page-->
            <div class="bar1"></div>
            <div class="bar2"></div>
            <div class="bar3"></div>
        </div>

        <ul id="menu">
            <li><a>Home</a></li> <!--contains lniks to the other pages-->
            <li><a>New York</a></li>
            <li><a>Hawaii</a></li>
            <li><a>Texas</a></li>
            <li><a>Other</a></li>
        </ul>

        <h1>Florida Travel Guide</h1>

        <div class="headerContent"> <!--div is used to help with css-->

            <div class="introText">
                <h2>Intro to Florida</h2>

                <p>
                    Florida, also known as the 'Sunshine State' is one of America's most
                    coastal locations, with no point more than 60 miles from the sea.
                    That means there's no shortage of fun water activity to enjoy!
                    But that's not all, Florida is home to various other attractions
                    with museums, landmarks and one of the most diverse ecosystems in
                    the states. Whether you want to enjoy the warm waves, marvel at
                    the wildlife or take in the scenery, Florida is the place for you!
                </p>
            </div>

            <img src="floridaScape.jpg" alt="headerImage" class="headerImage"> <!--imports the header image-->

        </div>

    </header>

    <section class="attraction"> <!--section is used to divide the page into 3 sections not including the header and footer-->

        <h2>Main Attractions</h2>

        <article>

            <video width="100%" height="auto" controls autoplay muted loop> <!--imports a video and sets it to autoplay, mute and loop-->
                <source src="miamiBeach.mp4" type="video/mp4">
            </video>

            <div class="beachText">
                <h2>Miami Beach</h2>

                <p>
                    Miami Beach is actually its own municipality connected to mainland
                    Miami by bridges. It holds the largest collection of Art Deco
                    buildings, with over 800 across the city. There are several beaches
                    scattered all over, with one for each of your wants. There are
                    beaches with resorts, ones for nightlife and of course the classic
                    quiet and relaxing locations.
                </p>
            </div>

        </article>

        <article>

            <div class="disneyText">
                <h2>Walt Disney World Resort</h2>

                <p>
                    Better known as Disney World, this world famous theme park has
                    something for everyone. Four theme parks, two water parks and
                    29,000 hotel rooms all themed after iconic Disney media all come
                    together to make an unforgettable experience for anybody to enjoy.
                    Each year the roster of characters and locations only grows, so
                    now is the perfect time to visit!
                </p>
            </div>

            <img src="disneyLand.jpg" alt="disneylandImage" class="disneyPic">

        </article>

        <article>

            <img src="gatorland.jpg" alt="gatorlandImage" class="gatorPic">

            <div class="gatorText">
                <h2>Gatorland</h2>

                <p>
                    Gatorland is a 110 acre theme and wildlife park situated in the
                    south of Florida. It's known as the "Alligator Capital" of America
                    due to the sheer amount of alligators and crocodiles you can find.
                    This park is perfect for spotting some of Florida's natural
                    inhabitants for any nature lovers. It has also been the backdrop
                    for many films such as a 1984 Indiana Jones flick.
                </p>
            </div>

        </article>

    </section>

    <section>

        <h2>Sounds of Florida</h2>

        <p>
            Across Florida, there are plenty of sights and Sounds that will leave you
            speechless. Since we've seen some of said sights, here are some of the
            best audial delights that the Sunshine State can offer you.
        </p>

        <ul class="sound-list"> <!--creates a list for the 'sounds of florida' to be placed in-->

            <li>
                <h3>Ocean Waves</h3>

                <audio controls>
                    <source src="Oceanwaves.mp3" type="audio/mpeg"> <!--imports an audio file into the page-->
                </audio>
            </li>

            <li>
                <h3>Tree Frogs</h3>

                <audio controls>
                    <source src="frogs.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
                </audio>
            </li>

            <li>
                <h3>Inland Birds</h3>

                <audio controls>
                    <source src="landBirds.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
                </audio>
            </li>

            <li>
                <h3>Tropical Birds</h3>

                <audio controls>
                    <source src="tropicalBirds.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
                </audio>
            </li>

        </ul>

    </section>

    <section class="otherPlaces">

        <div class="otherText">

            <h2>Other Major Attractions</h2>

            <table style="margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto;"> <!--creates a table for the loactions and target audiences to be placed into-->

                <tr>
                    <th>Location</th>
                    <th>Target Audience</th>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>Universal Orlando</td>
                    <td>Thrill Seekers</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>Sea World</td>
                    <td>Animal Lovers</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>Lego Land</td>
                    <td>Families</td>
                </tr>

            </table>

        </div>

        <div class="scrollWheel"> <!--puts 3 images into a section in order to make a scroll wheel in css-->
            <img src="universal.jpg" alt="Universal">
            <img src="seaworld.jpg" alt="Sea World">
            <img src="legoLand.jpg" alt="Lego Land">
        </div>

    </section>

    <footer>

        <h2>Florida Travel Guide</h2>

        <p>
            Explore Florida's beaches, wildlife, attractions, and culture.
        </p>

        <p>
            <a href="#top">Back to Top</a> |<!--brings the user back to the top of the body-->
